          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP638 - Glendon&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We enjoyed the nearby Perogy monument.  Thanks for the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="636502854">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="54.250483" lon="-111.154000" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-09-09T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="59862">j2d2</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP638 - Glendon&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I was searching away as Mommy RR was Pokemoning, and then I finally found the hole just as she arrived.  All the grass made it really hard to find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks OFTH&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="620965133">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-23T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3355355">CachingCarolandHugh</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP638 – Glendon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posted: N54º 15.029  W111º 09.240

Elevation: 586.6 M&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPSr:    N 54º 15.028  W111º 09.247

Elevation: 580&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Could not get the Number or the year after the rain that we'd had hear for the previous 3 days as the hole had 6 inches of water in it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We had come up to Cold Lake on Tuesday July 5th to attend the Sails, Rails &amp; Tails 2016 (WESTCAN6) Mega event. Then stayed over at the RV park we were at, for another week to do some more caching and take in the Cold Lake Air Show the following weekend. We logged a lot of caches found and with the satellite event in places like Elk Point and Glendon were also able to find some of the Brass Caps in Cold Lake and area.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This cap was found after attending the &quot;Yum Yum  - Pyrogies&quot; event in Glendon on Wed. July 6th.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;...CachingCarolandHugh &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_approve.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="619223449">
          <groundspeak:date>2016-07-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP638 Glendon&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first thing we did in Glendon was to visit the world's largest pyrogy.  Sadly, it was all fenced in.  Perhaps it had started to get into trouble?  Go bad?  Then we had to come and visit this cap.  Even with no marker post in the middle of a patch of grass, it was a quick find and needed only a little cleaning with a wet rag, courtesy of a nearby puddle.  Just as we returned to our vehicle another pulled up on the side street and out got gumbyphv.  Apparently, he was following behind us finding the caps we had so labouriously dug up and cleaned off.  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;  We enjoyed a chat with him and his wife.  Hopefully, he got done with the cap before the rain shower that caught us at the last cache stop in town, but really, all he had to do was take pictures.  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;  Thanks for the brass cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
    </groundspeak:cache>
